+For a MegaBench `multi-agent` run, setting
+`VIBESYS_MEGABENCH_NCU_MCP_COMMAND` to the absolute `ncu-mcp-server` executable
+adds the external `ncu_mcp` server to implementer sessions only. With the
+variable unset, no server is attached. Set `NCU_PATH` to the case checkout's
+absolute `megabench/integrations/ncu_capture.sh` path to capture only the profiler window.
+The executable's virtual environment, the MegaBench Python environment, and
+the real CUDA toolkit directory must be readable in the local agent sandbox;
+grant them with colon-separated `VIBESYS_AGENT_SANDBOX_ALLOW` entries. For an
+editable `ncu-mcp` install, also grant its `src` directory because the venv's
+`.pth` file imports the package from that external path. Put the
+real CUDA `bin` directory (for example `/usr/local/cuda-13.1/bin`) in `PATH`,
+not the `/usr/local/cuda/bin` symlink, which bubblewrap cannot create inside
+the sandbox.
